      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fort Defiance, built by General “Mad” Anthony Wayne in August 1794, sits where the Auglaize and Maumee rivers meet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Defiance%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes straight from that fort, honoring Wayne’s 1794 stronghold.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Defiance%2C_Ohio"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Defiance lies at the confluence of the Auglaize and Maumee rivers, roughly 55 miles southwest of Toledo.",
